==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Shingen''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Shingen''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Shingen is basically a Dark/Alien nuker. While he only attacks these traits, he absolutely eviscerates them and will be extremely helpful in Alien/Dark heavy stages.

Due to his long attack animation, he will often miss his targets, meaning that he is more effective when there are not many units to support him or against enemies with few knockbacks.

While his slow attacks leave him to be undesirable, he can almost always be useful in all [[Into the Future]] stages and later [[Stories of Legend]] stages, as well as Cats of the Cosmos on occasion.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Shingen has better range and damage, which, combined, improve his effectiveness by a lot. Thanks to these, Shingen is now able to hit more enemies, plus he has more time to hit them before he is reached. In addition, his improved health can make him work better against [[Tackey]] and the like.

==='''Talents'''===
[[Talents]] allow Immortal Shingen to target [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]], which pretty much increases his usability to 50%, if not more due to the abundance of mix-trait stages, and how he can outrange most short-ranged angel pushers, even reaching into the mid-rangers with [[Angelic Sleipnir]]. Attack Buff and the Talent Orb slot can be used to further improve Shingen's damage, which, considering how strong this unit is, can never be a bad idea. Also note that an Attack Orb would increase Shingen's damage by a larger amount than your usual damage dealer, as he relies directly on his base attack power, rather than a modifier like massive damage.

Cost Down, Barrier Breaker and HP Buff are definitely nice, but only invest in them if you see yourself using Shingen a lot, as these are pricey for how rarely they make a difference. Of note is that, should you invest in Shingen's Attack Buff and get him to Level 60, he'll begin dealing enough damage to break even the barriers of [[UltraBaaBaa]] and [[Youcan]], thus making Barrier Breaker almost completely worthless, so do not get that talent if you plan to use your Dark Catseyes on him.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
With these, Shingen can target Red, Zombie, and Aku enemies, though each trait is unlocked separately. These talents are great, and may be worth the Catseyes and NP. These talents are useful for mixed-trait stages with the traits that Shingen already targets.

Red enemies would normally be the strongest showing, though Red enemies have already been powercrept by the plethora of non-Uber anti-Reds. This talent would be unnecessary on account of it being overkill, though a level 60+ Shingen can still shine against some of the beefier Red enemies when crowd-controlling options are limited. However, against enemies that can be crowd-controlled, such as [[Bore]] and [[J.K. Bun Bun]], he is largely unnecessary due to the plethora of non-Uber options to take care of them. Notably, he can outrange [[Red EnerG]] and mostly stay safe from his Surge, and this is one of the few uses where Shingen shines due to a lack of competition and not just brute power. Additionally, if Red EnerG pushes, then the attack will allow Shingen to reposition to safety, as a Shingen at such a high level would have the HP to handle it.

Zombie enemies are considerably less powercrept and generally more difficult to defeat than Red enemies, so this talent would be quite useful. However, this talent does not come with Z-Killer or Soulstrike, which affects Shingen's compatibility against these enemies and even makes those enemies more difficult should they be given the chance to revive, as they likely will revive if a powerful hit from Shingen finishes them off. While this sounds like a deal-breaker on paper, Shingen's constant, high damage attacks and high bulk allow him to be a strong force against Zombies in practice, and he will usually kill Zombies again after they revive. The lack of Z-Killer is only a severe hindrance against Zombies that revive infinitely, such as [[Zamelle]]. A more pressing concern is that Shingen's lack of knockbacks would affect his survivability against Zombie enemies, as burrowing Zombies could either cut out your meatshield line or appear right on top of Shingen. However, this is another good talent to unlock.

Aku enemies are a more favorable matchup than Red or Zombie enemies. Shingen has no Shield Pierce, though he can still work well against Akus without shields or just use brute force to break them anyhow. Even then, he can be paired with Shield Piercers in several occasions. However, his compatibility is affected by the complete lack of immunities, as Aku enemies often throw waves and surges around every corner they touch. However, Shingen's strong bulk allows him to just tank most surges, though this lack of Surge immunity would make him unviable in aggresssive surge spam stages. If you already plan on boosting Shingen to level 60, then this would be the most worthwhile Ultra Talent despite its limitations.

==='''Orb'''===
Either Strengthen or Attack Up Orbs vs any target trait.
