==Trivia==
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Takeda Shingen the ability to target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]].
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Takeda Shingen was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Nemeses (Removed Combo)|Nemeses]] and [[Big Fans (Removed Combo)|Big Fans]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]], Immortal Shingen was one of the few [[:Category:Cats with Ultra Talents|Cats with Ultra Talents]] to lack a second [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]] slot.
*Although Immortal Shingen's description states that he is using the Cat Sword, it is actually an axe.
*Takeda Shingen does the third highest damage out of all cats (EN version), behind only [[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]/[[Heracrist (Uber Rare Cat)|Heracrist]] (tied for 2nd), and [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]].
*The marks on Takeda Shingen's sword in the Japanese version are different than the English version, with the Japanese one having the marks "風林火山" on it (Wind, Forest, Fire, Mountain (A reference to the Takeda Crest)) on all the form's weapons and meaningless marks/signs on the English version.
**This makes him one of the few cats with regional differences.
**Both the English and Japanese versions of [[The Battle Cats POP!]] used his spritesheet from BCJP.
*Takeda Shingen was the first unit to have the [[Attacks Only]] ability.
*This Cat is a tribute to the eponymous Japanese warlord, [[wikipedia:Takeda Shingen|Takeda Shingen]].
**Takeda Shingen and [[wikipedia:Uesugi Kenshin|Uesugi Kenshin]] are known for their rivalry during the Sengoku period. They were enemies in multiple battles, yet they had mutual respect for each other.
*Takeda Shingen's descriptions were not changed in The Battle Cats POP! to remove mentions of his [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] targeting, despite the fact that Alien enemies aren't present in that version.

